<title>GERMANY: VW grp car sales up 18.1 pct in January.</title>
<headline>VW grp car sales up 18.1 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>WOLFSBURG, Germany 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Volkswagen AG said group sales of vehicles surged 18.1 percent in January to 329,300 units compared with 278,866 in the year-ago period of January 1996.</p>
<p>Volkswagen said all five of its brand names within the group contributed to the higher sales.</p>
<p>The carmaker also said it expected to maintain its international market position despite &quot;rather subdued&quot; industry conditions.</p>
<p>The carmaker gave the following breakdown of its sales over the sales levels in January 1996:</p>
<p>    Volkswagen passenger cars		212,500 vs 185,670</p>
<p>    Volkswagen trucks			  26,300  vs 18,920</p>
<p>    Audi					   43,800  vs 33,253</p>
<p>    Seat					   28,500  vs 24,161</p>
<p>    Skoda					  18,100  vs 16,862</p>
<p>Volkswagen also gave the following breakdown of regional sales figures compared with January 1996:</p>
<p>    Western Europe			     192,300 vs 177,557</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>	--Germany				  73,300  vs 71,870</p>
<p>	--Other areas of Europe		119,00  vs 105,687</p>
<p>    Eastern Europe			     18,400  vs 14,309</p>
<p>    Japan					  4,000   vs 2,951</p>
<p>    China					  22,600  vs 14,114</p>
<p>    South Africa				 5,500   vs 4,346</p>
<p>    North America				16,000  vs 13,238</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>	--United States			  11,000  vs 8,801</p>
<p>    Brazil					 57,400  vs 39,593</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
